As required by section 4(b) of the Apache License, the following are the
significant changes made to the original work:

  - Express 4 compatibility removed; the project targets Express 5 only.
  - Public API documented, and type checked from those annotations.
  - Router dispatch reworked so a chain of N middlewares allocates one promise
    instead of N, and the mount stack is no longer walked on every hop.
  - Request bodies are collected in native code by uWebSockets.js when the
    length is known, with the size limit enforced before any byte reaches
    JavaScript, instead of being copied once per chunk and again on
    concatenation; the body parsers read the few headers they need from the
    raw header entries and bind the caller's async context only when a read
    actually goes asynchronous.
  - Empty request bodies now produce the same value each Express body parser
    produces, rather than being skipped.
  - Routes whose path is a literal are registered as native uWebSockets.js
    routes, with their path and method handed to the request as
    registration-time constants.
  - sendFile answers small unchanged files from a stat-validated cache, and
    concurrent reads of the same file are coalesced.
  - The query string parser is vendored from fast-querystring and answers on a
    bare null prototype, matching how Express displays parsed queries.
  - Express 5's own test suite runs against Fulmine as a CI gate, from a
    pinned checkout of Express.
  - The app is callable as a request listener, so http.createServer(app),
    supertest and anything else that invokes an app directly keeps working
    through a node:http shim.
  - Routing rebuilt on Express 5 semantics: its path matcher, case-insensitive
    matching by default, req.route, and assigning req.url inside a middleware
    re-routes the rest of the stack.
  - The routes listen() can read are compiled into one handler, with an overlap
    analysis deciding which of them may skip the middleware chain, and a
    self-check mode that serves the same application twice to show the compiled
    path answers as the chain it stands in for.
  - ETags are generated in this package rather than by the etag module, and an
    "etag methods" setting limits them to the methods it names.
  - express.compression() added, the compression module's middleware built in: a
    body that arrives whole is compressed in one call, and partial content is
    left alone.
  - express.serverTiming() added, which reports on the response how the request
    was routed.
  - express.static serves the .br and .gz twins of a file with preCompressed.
  - app.ws() serves websockets on the same port, with an upgrade hook and the
    request on the socket.
  - express({ cluster: "auto" }) forks one worker per core on the same port.
  - express.Route and express.testing added, the second one asserting what
    listen() decided about a route.
  - X-Powered-By is not sent unless the application asks for it, and the header
    methods, res.flushHeaders and the node members that were missing are filled
    in.
  - An adapter for NestJS ships as fulmine.js/nest.
  - A fulmine command added: it profiles and explains what listen() worked out
    about each route, verifies the machine, migrates a project, and prints the
    differences from Express.
  - Random applications are generated and compared against Express round by
    round, with the request bytes, the methods that compute a header value and
    keep-alive sequences each having their own fuzzer, and applications built on
    four frameworks run as an integration suite.
  - Releases are built and published to npm from CI.
  - Benchmark harness reworked: wrk replaced by autocannon so the suite runs
    anywhere Node does, NODE_ENV is set, load errors and response validation are
    no longer discarded, rows bounded by shared work are labelled, and scenarios
    were added for request shapes that were not covered.
  - listen() and close() aligned with Express: the callback runs on the next
    tick, and what listen() returns reports address(), listening and the
    'listening' and 'close' events.
  - Linting, formatting and commit hooks added.

